{
 "id": "Matrices-Inverses-Properties",
 "title_en": "Properties of the inverse",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "k": "p",
   "t": {
    "en": "The following are some algebraic properties of matrix inverses.",
    "sha": "d69b90e7760c",
    "zh": ""
   }
  },
  {
   "k": "box",
   "env": "proposition",
   "title": {
    "en": "Properties of the inverse",
    "sha": "a972c8b2b7b1",
    "zh": ""
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "k": "p",
     "t": {
      "en": "Let $A$ and $B$ be $n \\times n$-matrices, $I$ the $n\\times n$-identity matrix. Then the following hold.",
      "sha": "54f8b5b1849f",
      "zh": ""
     }
    },
    {
     "k": "list",
     "ordered": true,
     "items": [
      [
       {
        "k": "p",
        "t": {
         "en": "$I$ is invertible and $I^{-1} = I$.",
         "sha": "81979d0c54e5",
         "zh": ""
        }
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "k": "p",
        "t": {
         "en": "If $A$ and $B$ are invertible then $AB$ is invertible, and $(AB)^{-1} = B^{-1}A^{-1}$.",
         "sha": "b20689866e61",
         "zh": ""
        }
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "k": "p",
        "t": {
         "en": "If $A$ is invertible then so is $A^{-1}$, and $(A^{-1})^{-1} = A$.",
         "sha": "7bd8b812828b",
         "zh": ""
        }
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "k": "p",
        "t": {
         "en": "If $A$ is invertible then so is $A^k$, and $(A^k)^{-1} = (A^{-1})^k$.",
         "sha": "e87173bb6092",
         "zh": ""
        }
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "k": "p",
        "t": {
         "en": "If $A$ is invertible and $p$ is a non-zero scalar, then $pA$ is invertible and $(pA)^{-1} = \\frac{1}{p}A^{-1}$.",
         "sha": "f771f4bb8453",
         "zh": ""
        }
       }
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "exercises": [],
 "title_zh": "逆矩阵的性质"
}
